+# PatcherSupportPkg
+
+Repo dedicated to Apple binaries used for patching macOS to run with legacy hardware.
+------------------
+![GitHub all releases](https://img.shields.io/github/downloads/hackdoc/PatcherSupportPkg/total?color=white&style=plastic)
+------------------
+## Sources:
+
+* [ASentientBot](https://github.com/ASentientBot):
+  * Mojave, Catalina and Big Sur Graphics Acceleration Patches
+* [dosdude1](https://github.com/dosdude1):
+  * Brightness Control for El Capitan
+  * Mojave and Catalina Graphics Acceleration Patches
+* [Ausdauersportler](https://github.com/Ausdauersportler):
+  * Linking fixes for AppleIntelSNBGraphicsFB and AMDRadeonX3000.kext
+* [Jackluke](https://github.com/jacklukem), EduCovas, [DhinakG](https://github.com/DhinakG), [Khronokernel](https://github.com/khronokernel)
+  * Determining patch set for Intel HD 4000
+
+
+## Optional 26x86 artifact receipt
+
+The receipt path records an already-produced local artifact; it does not run
+payload cleanup, binary signing, shader patching, or macOS installation.
+All target values are explicit. A receipt never claims compatibility or boot.
+
+```sh
+python3 ci.py --artifact-receipt --artifact /path/to/existing.pkg --output /path/to/new-receipt.json --role root-support-package --macos-major 26 --os-build 25A354 --architecture x86_64 --runtime-abi verified-adapter-or-compiler-abi --license-file /path/to/payload-license.txt
+```
+
+The `26x86.support-artifact/1` schema binds the artifact SHA-256, exact macOS
+build, declared host architecture, runtime ABI, current source revision and
+license text SHA-256. Source working-tree modifications are reported. The
+license argument describes the actual payload terms; this tool grants no
+redistribution rights and does not copy the payload. Output creation is
+exclusive. Existing receipts are not overwritten.
+
+For `gpu-compiler-abi`, the actual compiler binary is mandatory and hashed.
+GPU bytecode is not a native CPU kext/dylib abstraction. The receipt can be
+checked with `artifact_receipt.verify_receipt` or the identical consumer in
+26x86 `x86.patch.artifact_receipt`, using independently selected build/ABI
+values and local artifact/license/compiler files.
